                    briefing_text_r2:       `Before you choose anyone, design the <em>process</em> by which the decision will be made and seen to be made. Set <strong>weighted criteria</strong> in advance, decide how candidates and the team get <strong>voice</strong>, check bias, and document an auditable, correctable record. You face the trade-off between <strong>speed</strong> — the role opens 1 May — and the legitimacy a fuller process buys. The research is blunt: people accept an unfavourable outcome far more readily when the process is voice-rich, consistent and transparent.`,
